WEBVTT

00:07.820 --> 00:12.240
Les Misérables

00:07.820 --> 00:12.240
A Girl Named Cosette

00:08.770 --> 00:11.780
Beyond the wind

00:12.240 --> 00:15.660
The wind blows

00:12.240 --> 00:15.660
Kaze ga fuki nuketeku

00:15.660 --> 00:22.290
over the daisies blooming over the stone pavement

00:15.660 --> 00:22.290
Ishidatami ni saku hinagiku

00:22.290 --> 00:25.830
I held my knees

00:22.290 --> 00:25.830
Hiza wo tsuite

00:25.830 --> 00:31.300
and gazed at the flowers

00:25.830 --> 00:31.300
Jitto mitsumeteta

00:31.300 --> 00:35.010
Far away, very far away

00:31.300 --> 00:35.010
Tooku haruka tooku

00:35.010 --> 00:41.640
A gentle voice is calling me

00:35.010 --> 00:41.640
Watashi wo yobu yasashii koe

00:41.640 --> 00:45.270
Let's go look for it

00:41.640 --> 00:45.270
Sagashii ni yukou

00:45.270 --> 00:51.030
Even if we wander aimlessly

00:45.270 --> 00:51.030
Attemonai keredo

00:51.030 --> 00:55.780
The rain comes down

00:51.030 --> 00:55.780
Doushaburi no ame

00:55.780 --> 01:00.530
on a lonely morning

00:55.780 --> 01:00.530
Hitoribocchi no asa

01:00.530 --> 01:05.040
But look, beyond the clouds

01:00.530 --> 01:05.040
Demo hora kumo no mukou

01:05.040 --> 01:09.630
the sunlight is peering at us

01:05.040 --> 01:09.630
Hizashi ga nozoiteruyo

01:09.630 --> 01:12.000
Wipe away your tears

01:09.630 --> 01:12.000
Namida fuite

01:12.000 --> 01:14.970
Look forward

01:12.000 --> 01:14.970
Mae wo muite

01:14.970 --> 01:19.260
and summon all of your strength

01:14.970 --> 01:19.260
Ashimoto chikara komete

01:19.260 --> 01:21.600
Let's walk

01:19.260 --> 01:21.600
Aruite yukou

01:21.600 --> 01:23.970
I'm sure we will make it

01:21.600 --> 01:23.970
Kitto yukeru

01:23.970 --> 01:31.360
The road, the road, continues on...

01:23.970 --> 01:31.360
Michi wa michi wa tsuzuku yo...

01:31.360 --> 01:34.400
forever...

01:31.360 --> 01:34.400
Dokomademo

02:01.890 --> 02:02.850
Cosette!

02:04.970 --> 02:05.720
Coming!

02:07.230 --> 02:08.850
We don't have any water left!

02:09.650 --> 02:11.810
Didn't I say to keep the bucket full?!

02:12.520 --> 02:13.690
I'm sorry.

02:13.690 --> 02:16.280
Geez... what a halfhearted child.

02:19.860 --> 02:24.370
Hey, Cosette. Since you're fetching the water, why
not use the bigger one over there to fetch it?

02:26.250 --> 02:27.830
Won't it be able to carry more water?

02:27.830 --> 02:29.830
Eh? Using that big bucket?

02:30.290 --> 02:31.960
That one is too big.

02:31.960 --> 02:33.290
Then, I'm going.

02:43.300 --> 02:45.310
What's with her attitude?

02:46.020 --> 02:46.850
Mother!

02:47.060 --> 02:49.440
Who cares what she uses?

02:53.730 --> 02:54.900
Cosette!

02:57.780 --> 02:58.320
Bread!

02:59.200 --> 03:00.240
It looks tasty.

03:15.630 --> 03:16.840
Chou Chou, we're going!

03:23.590 --> 03:25.430
How long are you going to take to fetch water?

03:25.720 --> 03:27.260
Hurry up and do the cleaning for the second floor!

03:27.470 --> 03:28.020
Yes.

03:48.330 --> 03:52.040
Wheat... harvest... prices collapse...

03:54.920 --> 03:55.750
Cosette!

03:57.500 --> 03:58.170
What's the matter?

04:04.840 --> 04:07.220
Éponine said to have them all washed!

04:07.470 --> 04:09.270
You have to wash mine and Gavroche's as well!

04:17.770 --> 04:22.740
Lost Éponine

04:23.200 --> 04:24.990
Chou Chou! Hey, Chou Chou!

04:33.790 --> 04:35.460
Cosette, what's this?

04:35.790 --> 04:36.500
It's a newspaper.

04:38.590 --> 04:42.090
I can only read a bit of it, but there are a lot of things written on it.

04:42.210 --> 04:44.220
What is written on it?

04:44.220 --> 04:49.430
Um... Like this year's winter is apparently
very cold, or there is a shortage of wheat.

04:49.890 --> 04:52.180
Or that there is going to be a big Mass at the church.

04:54.560 --> 04:56.020
Hey, you two!

04:56.020 --> 04:57.900
Are you the children of this inn?!

04:57.900 --> 04:58.690
Yes!

04:59.190 --> 05:01.530
Oh my, welcome.

05:02.190 --> 05:03.360
Are you staying overnight?

05:03.690 --> 05:05.150
Yes. Do you have any vacant rooms?

05:05.150 --> 05:06.610
Of course, we have vacant rooms.

05:14.830 --> 05:17.790
I'm deeply sorry, we're pretty booked at the moment.

05:18.290 --> 05:22.250
Um... we still have one vacant room.

05:22.250 --> 05:23.590
So, how much is it?

05:24.340 --> 05:25.880
It's 5 francs for the room.

05:25.880 --> 05:26.880
It's expensive.

05:26.880 --> 05:29.800
How can it be? That's our inn's best room, Monsieur.

05:29.800 --> 05:31.390
It's the rates around here.

05:31.390 --> 05:33.600
I understand. I will take it.

05:33.970 --> 05:35.350
Thank you very much.

05:35.560 --> 05:37.270
Here, please come this way.

05:37.520 --> 05:38.810
Are you coming here for business?

05:38.810 --> 05:41.190
Yeah. I just came back from Paris.

05:42.070 --> 05:42.900
Paris...

05:58.920 --> 06:03.500
These are goods of excellent quality. Can you please pay me a lot for these?

06:04.710 --> 06:08.380
No matter how well they're made, you have already worn them out.

06:08.880 --> 06:11.550
Well, I'll give you 10 francs for these.

06:12.350 --> 06:14.890
A little more. Can you give me more?

06:16.730 --> 06:19.020
Oh... that's a well-made pendant.

06:19.270 --> 06:21.190
If you sell that too, I can give you more...

06:23.520 --> 06:27.610
No, this is something precious which my mother gave me.

06:27.990 --> 06:30.610
Then, I can't give you any more.

06:40.920 --> 06:44.290
I'm sorry. I only have this to pay for the rent.

06:44.460 --> 06:46.420
What? So little again?

06:46.710 --> 06:47.880
It's troublesome.

06:48.050 --> 06:48.880
I'm sorry.

06:50.010 --> 06:54.350
I will wait for another three days. If you still
don't pay up, then you will be evicted.

07:03.690 --> 07:04.770
Fantine.

07:05.020 --> 07:06.570
He said he'll wait for another three days.

07:07.320 --> 07:12.200
This is distressing. The weather is turning colder, and if you're evicted now...

07:15.990 --> 07:17.700
I'll go out for a while.

07:20.290 --> 07:21.420
Please.

07:23.330 --> 07:25.290
I'll do anything. So I beg you!

07:25.670 --> 07:29.420
Well... But right now we have no work to give you to do...

07:30.470 --> 07:33.010
How about that? Can you let me do that?

07:34.090 --> 07:35.260
Oh, those?

07:35.640 --> 07:39.180
That is the work attire of the bread factory, but...

07:39.180 --> 07:41.270
They said they want them done in three days.

07:41.270 --> 07:42.440
Three days?

07:42.940 --> 07:46.570
It's absurd, right? I will just ask them to look for other tailors to do-

07:46.570 --> 07:47.230
I will do them.

07:48.480 --> 07:49.530
Please let me do them!

07:54.320 --> 07:55.780
Eh? You've to get them done in three days?

07:56.160 --> 07:59.700
I've promised the shop owner. I can't back off now.

08:01.660 --> 08:04.040
It'd be better if I help out.

08:04.040 --> 08:08.630
You don't have to. You've got a lot of buttons to sew, don't you?

08:17.550 --> 08:19.140
Here, drink up.

08:19.140 --> 08:20.720
Thank you.

08:22.140 --> 08:26.810
But it's really huge. Paris is the biggest city in France after all.

08:26.810 --> 08:30.610
So... So, what kind of clothes do the Parisians wear?

08:30.610 --> 08:32.900
Are they those stylish clothes with a lot of lace?

08:32.900 --> 08:37.740
Oh, that's right. Parisians are all fashion-conscious
and they all wear flamboyant clothing.

08:37.740 --> 08:39.330
...With a lot of lace.

08:40.080 --> 08:43.410
As for me, an old countryside bumpkin like me would feel interior.

08:44.370 --> 08:46.830
What countryside bumpkin?

08:47.000 --> 08:51.670
My wife, my children, and I have not stepped out of this village.

08:51.670 --> 08:55.720
That's right. We're running this inn so we don't get many chances to go out.

08:57.680 --> 09:00.970
But even for me, I have gone out once a month to do business.

09:02.140 --> 09:06.560
Oh right. The market there is lively and fun in the morning.

09:06.560 --> 09:08.650
The market? What is sold there?

09:08.650 --> 09:09.900
They sell all kinds of things.

09:09.900 --> 09:14.110
For starters, vegetables, fish, milk, flowers, poultry, and even water.

09:14.900 --> 09:16.240
They sell water too?!

09:16.320 --> 09:18.320
It's because water is valuable in Paris.

09:24.080 --> 09:25.000
Cosette.

09:26.870 --> 09:28.830
There are still customers here!

09:29.210 --> 09:30.170
Oh, I'm sorry.

09:31.380 --> 09:32.550
Why is she so-out of it?

09:33.170 --> 09:35.590
I'm sorry for flying into a rage.

09:35.590 --> 09:38.470
No, it's nothing. Haven't you eaten?

09:40.100 --> 09:41.220
I...

09:42.760 --> 09:44.980
This child will eat later.

09:45.180 --> 09:45.930
Really?

09:56.070 --> 09:58.490
This child isn't ours.

09:58.490 --> 10:00.740
A traveling woman left her in our care.

10:02.240 --> 10:03.950
Cosette, go to the other side.

10:05.290 --> 10:09.830
We're kindhearted, so we have taken care of her for 5 years already.

10:10.040 --> 10:12.750
So what? We're used to helping out others.

10:12.750 --> 10:20.550
Actually, in the Battle of Waterloo, I have valiantly fought
alongside the famous Emperor Napoleon as a sergeant.

10:20.680 --> 10:25.810
And during the battle, I risked my life to save a general who was shot.

10:25.810 --> 10:26.730
During that time...

10:26.730 --> 10:29.350
Hey, Monsieur, tell me more about Paris.

10:29.980 --> 10:31.270
What else does it have?

10:31.900 --> 10:33.440
Let's see...

10:33.940 --> 10:36.150
Paris has a lot of gardens.

10:36.150 --> 10:40.110
Lots of flowers bloom in these gardens and children are always playing games.

10:41.530 --> 10:42.570
What kind of games do they play?

10:43.080 --> 10:45.120
What kind of games do the children in Paris play?

10:45.120 --> 10:48.750
Let's see... Girls often played "l'arceau".

10:50.330 --> 10:52.580
What's "l'arceau"? What kind of a game is it?

10:52.710 --> 10:54.500
Well... let's see...

10:54.840 --> 10:56.170
There's a bell inside a hoop.

10:58.050 --> 11:01.470
If you use the stick to roll the hoop, the bell inside the hoop will ring.

11:01.470 --> 11:03.640
That's right. It's just as you have said.

11:03.930 --> 11:05.390
Why do you know?

11:05.390 --> 11:07.810
Have you played it before? Have you been to Paris?

11:08.730 --> 11:12.440
You're lying! How could you have been to Paris, Cosette?!

11:12.940 --> 11:14.360
I don't remember clearly...

11:15.190 --> 11:19.320
But my mother and I lived in a really big city when I was young.

11:19.950 --> 11:22.950
There were a lot of flowers. It was a really beautiful place.

11:24.370 --> 11:26.120
Isn't that Paris?!

11:26.910 --> 11:28.580
That can't be!

11:28.580 --> 11:31.040
This child came from a poor village.

11:31.040 --> 11:33.210
Yes! How could she have been to Pari-

11:32.790 --> 11:37.000
There was a big river. There were boats on it, and even people swimming in it.

11:37.000 --> 11:37.880
That's the Seine.

11:39.800 --> 11:44.470
There were also artists, singers, and dancers.

11:44.470 --> 11:48.100
You really did live in Paris before. I'm sure of it.

11:48.930 --> 11:49.640
Paris...

11:54.900 --> 11:55.400
Come here.

11:59.320 --> 12:00.610
You're not having any dinner tonight.

12:01.490 --> 12:03.700
I won't forgive you for speaking unnecessary things!

12:16.380 --> 12:18.210
I remembered it, Mother.

12:19.250 --> 12:21.970
My happy childhood when I lived in Paris.

12:49.330 --> 12:53.250
<i>Why would Cosette have been to Paris? I've never been there!</i>

12:55.040 --> 12:57.420
Éponine, what's wrong?

12:57.960 --> 12:58.500
Be quiet!

13:01.300 --> 13:03.170
Cosette! Cosette!

13:03.800 --> 13:05.800
Why are you slacking off?!

13:05.800 --> 13:08.680
Go and clean the stables and wash the clothes!

13:08.680 --> 13:09.260
Yes!

13:22.230 --> 13:23.070
Cosette.

13:23.690 --> 13:26.360
Oh, Mr. Customer. Are you leaving?

13:26.910 --> 13:31.620
No... I have something to say to you. Is it all right?

13:33.290 --> 13:36.920
May Gavorche come along? He's like my little brother.

13:36.920 --> 13:38.330
Yes, he may.

13:44.340 --> 13:46.970
I'd like to give this picture to you.

13:49.800 --> 13:50.430
This is...

13:51.390 --> 13:54.180
It's the river that I talked about yesterday!

13:54.180 --> 13:56.940
Yes. It's the Seine in Paris.

13:57.480 --> 13:58.310
Paris?

13:58.310 --> 14:00.270
You're giving this to me? Is it all right?

14:00.610 --> 14:05.570
Yes. I would like you to look at this and remember more about Paris.

14:05.780 --> 14:08.240
I'm so happy. Thank you very much.

14:08.610 --> 14:13.120
Also, these are sweets from a popular shop in Paris.

14:13.740 --> 14:14.540
I'll give them to the two of you.

14:22.670 --> 14:24.460
Éponine! Éponine!

14:24.460 --> 14:26.550
What is it? You could have knocked!

14:26.920 --> 14:28.630
You know, Cosette has...

14:32.510 --> 14:34.220
Now, hurry up and eat them.

14:34.470 --> 14:36.020
Eh? Right now?

14:36.390 --> 14:37.520
Yes! Hurry up!

14:42.650 --> 14:43.770
Mother, you see!

14:47.150 --> 14:48.820
Cosette! Gavroche!

14:48.900 --> 14:52.620
I gave some sweets from Paris that I had to the two of them.

14:53.330 --> 14:56.750
Unfortunately, I only had two sweets... It doesn't matter, right?

14:57.700 --> 14:58.620
Okay...

15:06.840 --> 15:10.720
It's going to get tougher from now on. You have to do your best.

15:11.760 --> 15:12.340
Yes!

15:13.600 --> 15:14.350
Farewell.

15:21.810 --> 15:25.320
Mother! Mother! Cosette even has a drawing of Paris!

15:26.070 --> 15:27.900
Dear, are you really going?

15:27.900 --> 15:30.610
Yeah. The price of wheat will rise.

15:31.360 --> 15:33.620
So I'm gonna invest with this money.

15:34.120 --> 15:36.410
But what if the price falls...

15:36.410 --> 15:37.490
Shut up!

15:37.740 --> 15:40.250
You have no say in what I do.

15:41.750 --> 15:43.500
Mother! What about the drawing of Paris?!

15:44.080 --> 15:46.000
Who cares about the drawing?

15:47.800 --> 15:50.420
All right then. I will look for it!

15:52.720 --> 15:53.470
The drawing of Paris...

15:54.590 --> 15:55.300
The drawing of Paris!

16:02.600 --> 16:03.770
I found it!

16:06.520 --> 16:07.730
What's this?

16:08.360 --> 16:09.530
This is Paris?

16:10.610 --> 16:11.900
What's the matter, Chou Chou?

16:13.070 --> 16:14.740
You cannot come inside of the house.

16:15.660 --> 16:16.490
Éponine...

16:20.160 --> 16:21.910
What's this?! This isn't Paris!

16:58.780 --> 17:02.910
<i>I'll go to Paris too. Even Cosette has been there before.</i>

17:04.370 --> 17:05.170
<i>Even I...</i>

17:06.250 --> 17:08.330
I'm smiling...

17:08.710 --> 17:10.210
I'm back now.

17:10.210 --> 17:11.880
Dear, there's trouble!

17:11.880 --> 17:12.510
What?!

17:12.630 --> 17:13.800
Éponine has...

17:14.220 --> 17:15.720
What? What has happened?

17:15.970 --> 17:19.180
The big bag and her change of clothes are gone!

17:19.180 --> 17:21.390
She also took her best outdoor clothes!

17:21.680 --> 17:24.310
What?! This means she ran away from home?

17:25.640 --> 17:29.810
She kept jabbering about Paris last night.

17:30.400 --> 17:32.650
So, she has gone to Paris?!

17:33.190 --> 17:34.690
I don't know...

17:35.490 --> 17:36.780
What should I do...

17:37.280 --> 17:39.990
Anyway, let's ask the people in the village to help search for her.

17:40.530 --> 17:41.870
Cosette, you search for her as well.

17:41.870 --> 17:42.450
Yes.

17:45.250 --> 17:48.750
Chou Chou, do you know which way Éponine had gone?

17:53.090 --> 17:54.670
Eh? That way?

18:02.060 --> 18:03.600
Did she really go this way?!

18:23.410 --> 18:24.540
It's scary...

18:25.040 --> 18:26.410
Save me...

18:37.300 --> 18:38.130
You're...

18:38.630 --> 18:39.380
Éponine!

18:39.380 --> 18:40.470
We found her.

18:43.930 --> 18:47.730
Umm... Éponine, what are you doing out here?

18:48.060 --> 18:51.060
What am I doing? It's none of your business.

18:51.560 --> 18:52.980
Were you going to Paris?

18:54.610 --> 18:56.440
I was planning to.

18:56.440 --> 18:58.110
But I lost my way.

18:58.110 --> 19:01.320
This is the route that you take to fetch the water.

19:01.910 --> 19:03.580
There's a well over there.

19:04.370 --> 19:07.790
It's strange that you got lost here.

19:08.580 --> 19:09.870
Be quiet! Be quiet!

19:09.870 --> 19:14.420
Anyway, let's go back home. The mistress
and the others are worried about you.

19:15.300 --> 19:17.260
I'm not going back with either of you.

19:17.800 --> 19:19.420
Leave me alone.

19:20.510 --> 19:21.220
But...

19:21.470 --> 19:25.100
Cosette, you don't have to be concerned with Éponine. Let's go back.

19:25.100 --> 19:26.260
But...

19:26.260 --> 19:28.220
It's getting dark!

19:45.160 --> 19:47.580
It's slippery here, so be careful.

20:31.540 --> 20:32.290
Éponine!

20:32.830 --> 20:34.290
Why did you run away from home...

20:34.460 --> 20:36.500
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

20:36.710 --> 20:38.710
Éponine... Thank goodness.

20:39.210 --> 20:42.760
I was worried. Where did you go?

20:43.050 --> 20:45.090
I got lost on the path in the forest.

20:49.060 --> 20:51.310
I'm tired, so I'm going to take a rest.

20:52.520 --> 20:54.310
What's with her? What a strange girl.

20:55.350 --> 20:59.150
We got everyone worried even though you all were busy...

21:02.900 --> 21:04.990
I'm really sorry, everyone.

21:08.070 --> 21:10.790
Fantine, you can't continue like this...

21:11.580 --> 21:12.500
I have to do this.

21:13.040 --> 21:14.460
I have to do it until the end.

21:17.130 --> 21:19.340
You can't just say you couldn't make them in time.

21:20.000 --> 21:22.460
I'm sorry. I'm really sorry.

21:22.920 --> 21:24.880
It's the reputation of our shop at stake.

21:25.340 --> 21:27.090
If this is the case, I can't pay you.

21:27.340 --> 21:31.470
How can that be... If you don't pay me, I will be evicted from my apartment.

21:31.680 --> 21:34.600
We might even lose our regular customer.

21:42.980 --> 21:46.240
Fantine... do you have a place to stay?

21:46.530 --> 21:48.610
I'm all right. You don't have to worry.

22:13.680 --> 22:16.680
ma maman (my mother)

22:17.640 --> 22:20.860
I like you very much, Mother

22:17.640 --> 22:20.860
Daisukiyo nee okaasan

22:21.520 --> 22:24.900
I love you, Mother

22:21.520 --> 22:24.900
Aishiteru nee okaasan

22:25.530 --> 22:29.360
Your warm inviting scent

22:25.530 --> 22:29.360
Atataku ii nioi

22:29.360 --> 22:32.700
My precious mother

22:29.360 --> 22:32.700
Taisetsuna okaasan

22:33.530 --> 22:36.620
As long as you call out to me

22:33.530 --> 22:36.620
Yobikakeru sore dake de

22:37.580 --> 22:40.790
It brings me joy, Mother

22:37.580 --> 22:40.790
Ureshii no nee okaasan

22:41.500 --> 22:45.550
My only mother

22:41.500 --> 22:45.550
Kono sekai ni tatta hitori

22:45.550 --> 22:48.630
in this world

22:45.550 --> 22:48.630
Watashi no okaasan

22:49.970 --> 22:51.840
Hug me tightly

22:49.970 --> 22:51.840
Dakishimete gyutto

22:51.840 --> 22:53.810
Kiss me gently

22:51.840 --> 22:53.810
Kisu wo shitte sotto

22:53.810 --> 23:01.520
Always be by my side

22:53.810 --> 23:01.520
Itsudemo watashi no soba ni ite ne

23:02.020 --> 23:04.770
On the path lined with chestnut trees

23:02.020 --> 23:04.770
Maronie no michi

23:04.770 --> 23:09.740
we walk hand-in-hand

23:04.770 --> 23:09.740
Futari te wo tori aruku

23:09.740 --> 23:13.450
If we sing together,

23:09.740 --> 23:13.450
Isshoni utaeba

23:13.450 --> 23:17.620
we can have fun with just that.

23:13.450 --> 23:17.620
Tanoshii ne sore dake de

23:17.910 --> 23:21.830
Bathing in the sunlight filtering through the canopy

23:17.910 --> 23:21.830
Komorebi no naka yureru

23:21.830 --> 23:25.840
